{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794500367,"nonce":"uOZVm9f/q32jAwH8+aoD1S69fAA=","message":"Kept callbacks landed in fc428c8fa593bd7d2ef84b9b17b58e17838042f5: [HxnKept] on a callback argument makes the binding return an hxn.Stream of what C calls it with, and [HxnIgnore=int|pointer] covers the registration function's return value. The trampoline copies the values, sends them, and returns [HxnStop] to C on every call. The registering object owns the sender and drops it after its C free function runs, which ends the stream; free or static functions and borrowed objects leak it. The importer now imports functions named like set/hook/listen as kept instead of skipping them. Tested with tally_listen and sqlite3's update and commit hooks on Ash (all modes), hxcpp, CPPIA and Emscripten (sqlite skipped there).","files":null}]}